Explain why unauthorised hacking is a crime even if no damage is done in your own words

Unauthorized hacking is a crime because it breaks the owner's right to control access to their systems. Even if no harm is done, the hacker enters without permission. This violates privacy and security. Just like it's illegal to enter someone's house without permission, it's also illegal to access a computer system without authorization, no matter if something is stolen or damaged.


